course: dictionary
lesson: 2695
title: The same, but in a different way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Differently is an adverb. It tells us how something is done, and it means in a way that is not the same as another way or as before. «Reading slowly or finding it hard to sit still is not the same as being stupid; many clever people learn differently.» So learn differently means learn in a different way. It does not mean learn badly.
explain: Look for the clue that shows what is being compared. In «Mandarin Chinese ... works very differently from English», the word from tells you what the comparison is. When you see differently from, ask yourself: different from what?
explain: Two people can see the same thing and remember it differently. «Mei's grandfather says Mao made China strong; her grandmother ... remembers it differently.» The two of them are not doing the same thing in their heads, so their memories do not match.
explain: Check a new word by putting your meaning into the sentence. «Step-siblings at the same school may act differently there than at home» means they act in a way that is not the same as at home. If your meaning fits, you are probably right.
fact: Differently is an adverb: it tells us how something is done or how it is.
fact: «Differently» means in a way that is not the same as another way or as before.
fact: Differently often comes with from, as in «works very differently from English».
fact: «Do things differently» means try another way instead of the usual way.
fact: In maths, «solve it differently» means find another method, which also helps you check your answer.
exercise: In «Reading slowly ... many clever people learn differently», what does learn differently mean? | Learn without any help at all | Learn only at night | Learn badly and slowly | *Learn in a way that is not the same as the usual way
exercise: Your maths teacher says, «Try to solve it differently.» What does she want you to do? | Write the answer in red | *Find another method to solve it | Give up and start again | Copy your friend's answer
exercise: «Mandarin Chinese works very differently from English.» What does differently from show? | *That the two languages are not the same | That English is written in pencil | That the two languages are exactly alike | That Mandarin is faster to speak
test: «For a while the street looked at Jamie differently.» What does this mean? | *The street looked at him in a new way, not the same as before | The street looked at him the same way as before | The street forgot his name | The street ran away from him
test: Which word means nearly the same as differently in the sense of in a way that is not the same? | Alike | Together | Always | *In another way
exam: Which sentence uses differently as an adverb to tell how something is done? | The school has a big red door and a tall tower | *Step-siblings may act differently at school than at home | Mao made China strong in the old days | Dad paid for the repair in the morning
